version: "2.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.18512473
repository-code: "https://github.com/Geoinformatics-Lab/PyGILE-Plus"
abstract: >-
  A computing environment, core curriculum and thematic modules for
  learning and applying geospatial analysis: a headless Docker environment
  combining SAGA GIS, GRASS GIS, WhiteboxTools and OTB with a Python
  geospatial and machine learning stack; the PyGILE core curriculum, a
  step-by-step course in Python and GIS for absolute beginners (39 lessons on
  real data from Nepal); and thematic modules built on it, starting with
  Landslide Susceptibility Mapping.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - GIS
  - remote sensing
  - Python
  - Docker
  - landslide susceptibility
  - education
  - Nepal
